INT. STEAMSHIP "MARIGOLD" - LOST AND FOUND OFFICE - DAY

A narrow room below decks, shelves of forgotten hats, umbrellas, a single ukulele. A porthole shows slow gray swells.

MR. FITCH, 50s, round spectacles, ledger in hand, presides behind a brass-railed counter. He is pleased with the order of the universe.

The door opens. BARNABY PLUMLEY, 40s, tweed, mustache like a pushbroom, enters with the confidence of a man who has never been refused. Behind him, ALOYSIUS FENN, 40s, also in tweed, also mustached, but nervous.

FITCH
Gentlemen. Something lost?

BARNABY
A trunk. Brown, brass corners, initialed B.P.

ALOYSIUS
Or A.F. It's our trunk.

FITCH
Two sets of initials?

BARNABY
We travel together.

ALOYSIUS
Not that way.

FITCH
I did not suggest a way.

Fitch opens the ledger. Runs a finger down the page.

FITCH (CONT'D)
Brown trunk, brass corners. Found on Deck C, yesterday.

BARNABY
That's the one.

FITCH
Did it contain anything unusual?

BARNABY
Shirts.

ALOYSIUS
And the Mortimer papers.

BARNABY
(sharp)
Shirts.

FITCH
Papers, you said?

ALOYSIUS
Shirts and papers. Mostly shirts.

Fitch produces a trunk from beneath the counter. Sets it down with ceremony. Unlatches it.

Inside: shirts. Neatly folded. One small leather folio.

FITCH (CONT'D)
Shirts. And a folio marked "Mortimer."

BARNABY
Yes. Splendid. We'll take it.

FITCH
I'll need a signature.

ALOYSIUS
Of course.

Fitch slides a form across. Barnaby reaches. Aloysius reaches. Their hands collide on the pen.

BARNABY
After you.

ALOYSIUS
No, you.

BARNABY
I insist.

ALOYSIUS
Then I insist more.

The door swings open again. HORTENSE VANDERWELL, 60s, fur stole in the tropics, enters with NELL, 9, in a sailor dress, clutching a stuffed walrus.

HORTENSE
Mr. Fitch! My daughter lost Sir Reginald!

NELL
He's right here, Grandmother.

HORTENSE
Then what are we doing here?

NELL
You said we'd get ice cream.

HORTENSE
Ah. So I did.

Fitch clears his throat.

FITCH
Madam, as you can see, I am engaged with two gentlemen.

HORTENSE
Two? I see one and a half.

BARNABY
I beg your pardon.

HORTENSE
Is the other one a ghost?

ALOYSIUS
I am quite solid, madam.

HORTENSE
So was my late husband. Look where it got him.

Silence. Fitch polishes his spectacles.

FITCH
Nell, was it? What lost thing do you seek?

NELL
Nothing. Grandmother told me to say we were looking for something so she could meet the two men with the matching mustaches.

HORTENSE
Nell!

NELL
You did.

HORTENSE
(to Barnaby)
Children invent the most extraordinary things.

BARNABY
Madam, we are not available for introductions.

ALOYSIUS
We are engaged.

BARNABY
To other people!

ALOYSIUS
Women!

HORTENSE
How very modern.

FITCH
Might I suggest we resolve the trunk?

BARNABY
Yes. The trunk.

ALOYSIUS
Please.

Fitch taps the folio.

FITCH
There is a problem, gentlemen.

BARNABY
Which is?

FITCH
This folio does not contain papers. It contains a deed.

ALOYSIUS
Barnaby.

BARNABY
Don't.

FITCH
To the Marigold.

HORTENSE
The ship?

FITCH
The ship. It appears that one of you, or perhaps both, has been selling it for some weeks, to various purchasers, on the open sea.

NELL
Can you sell a boat while you're on it?

HORTENSE
Apparently, dear. Apparently you can.

Barnaby and Aloysius look at each other. Then at the door.

BARNABY
After you.

ALOYSIUS
No, you.

They bolt together, wedged in the doorway. Fitch rings a brass bell. Somewhere above, a whistle blows.

NELL
Grandmother, can we still get ice cream?

HORTENSE
Child, we are going to buy the ship.
